From 677cb8790365106fff41e87fa3d1da9ae6774804 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Buckley <10402042+ryancbuckley@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:56:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Wasm stack limit checks (-Cllvm-args=wasm-stack-limit)

With the option, functions with a stack frame check it against the
__stack_limit global and trap instead of writing below the limit:
wasm has no guard pages to catch a thread outgrowing its stack. The
program must define the global (the playground's std does). Needs
clif-to-wasm 0.2.0, whose ObjectOptions is non-exhaustive and which
needs Cranelift 0.137.1.
